    content: [
      'Tenerife is one of the best places on the planet to look at the night sky. The summit of Mount Teide sits above the cloud layer at over 2,000 metres, the air is dry and stable, and light pollution is tightly controlled by law, which is why professional observatories were built here. For visitors, that adds up to a genuinely world-class stargazing experience, and it is one of the island\'s most underrated nights out.',
      'The reason the sky is so good comes down to geography. The Teide massif punches through the inversion layer that traps clouds and haze below, so the summit enjoys clear, steady air most nights of the year. Spain\'s Sky Law protects the darkness around the national park, and UNESCO has recognised the area as a prime astronomy site. On a moonless night you can see the Milky Way with the naked eye.',
      'You have two main ways to do it. The free option is to drive up into the Teide National Park after dark and stop at one of the designated viewpoints (miradores), bring warm layers, a red torch and a star app. The guided option is a stargazing tour: an astronomy guide brings telescopes, points out planets, nebulae and galaxies with a laser, and often includes hotel pick-up and a toast. For most visitors the guided tour is worth it, you see far more through a proper telescope than with the naked eye.',
      'Timing matters. Go on a night near the new moon for the darkest sky, check that the summit road is open (it occasionally closes for snow or wind), and dress for cold, it can be near freezing at altitude even when the coast is mild. Many tours combine a late-afternoon <a href="/en/activities/teide-cable-car-tour">cable car ride</a> with sunset and then stargazing, which is the perfect sequence.',
      'A Teide night pairs naturally with the rest of a Tenerife trip. Spend the day on the coast, a <a href="/en/activities/whale-watching-tenerife">whale watching trip</a> or a beach afternoon, then head up the mountain as the sun drops. And for the evenings when you stay at sea level, our self-guided <a href="/en/escape-game">outdoor escape games</a> keep the group entertained around the island. Browse everything on our <a href="/en/activities">things to do in Tenerife</a> page.',
    ],
