      "## Food, evenings and getting around",
      "The resort also has the best concentration of restaurants in the south, from beachfront seafood to fine dining in the hotels, plus the nearby <a href=\"/en/activities/flamenco-show-dinner-tenerife\">flamenco dinner show</a> for a classic Spanish evening. Nights here are about long dinners and cocktail terraces rather than clubs. Costa Adeje is roughly 10 to 15 minutes from Tenerife South airport and flows straight into <a href=\"/en/blog/playa-de-las-americas-tenerife-guide\">Playa de las Americas</a>, and it is the natural launch pad for west-coast trips to <a href=\"/en/blog/los-gigantes-tenerife-things-to-do\">Los Gigantes</a> and the Masca valley. See everything on our <a href=\"/en/activities\">things to do in Tenerife</a> page.",
